1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,990
太平洋上一大片海，
A huge patch of the Pacific

2
00:00:01,990 --> 00:00:04,730
一年之间，从绿色变成了蓝色。
went from green to blue in one year.

3
00:00:04,730 --> 00:00:06,110
蓝色不是更干净，
Blue doesn't mean cleaner.

4
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:07,270
而是饭没了。
It means the food is gone.

5
00:00:07,270 --> 00:00:10,420
NASA卫星测到，赤道太平洋的叶绿素，
A NASA satellite found chlorophyll in the equatorial Pacific

6
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:12,360
比一年前少了将近八成。
is down nearly 80% from a year ago.

7
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:16,070
罪魁祸首：可能是有记录以来最强的厄尔尼诺。
The culprit: maybe the strongest El Niño on record.

8
00:00:16,070 --> 00:00:19,190
今天的问题：太平洋发烧，关你啥事？
Today's question: the Pacific has a fever, why should you care?

9
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:21,520
认识一下小鳀，一条秘鲁鳀鱼。
Meet Andy, a Peruvian anchovy.

10
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,640
今天，它的饭碗要被端了。
Today, his dinner is about to vanish.

11
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:25,460
平时，赤道上的信风，
Normally, the trade winds along the equator

12
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:27,040
一直从东往西吹。
blow from east to west.

13
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:29,120
它把太阳晒热的表层海水，
They push the sun-warmed surface water

14
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:30,800
一路推到印尼那边。
all the way toward Indonesia.

15
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,660
就像你对着浴缸一直吹：
Like blowing across a bathtub nonstop:

16
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:34,460
热水全堆在了另一头。
the warm water piles up at the far end.

17
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:35,490
西边的海面，
So the sea surface in the west

18
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:37,660
因此比东边高出几十厘米。
sits tens of centimeters higher than the east.

19
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,290
东边，南美那一侧，
In the east, off South America,

20
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:41,230
深处的冷水就往上涌。
cold deep water wells up to replace it.

21
00:00:41,230 --> 00:00:43,630
冷水带着营养，养活浮游植物，
That cold water carries nutrients that feed plankton,

22
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:45,290
浮游植物养活小鳀。
and plankton feeds Andy.

23
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:47,260
反转一：信风一旦变弱，
Twist one: when the trade winds weaken,

24
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:49,360
浴缸里的水就晃回来了。
the bathtub water sloshes back.

25
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:52,020
暖水向东回流，像一床热被子，
Warm water flows east like a warm blanket,

26
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:53,660
把冷水盖在下面。
trapping the cold water below.

27
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:55,920
冷水上不来，营养上不来，
No cold water, no nutrients,

28
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:57,360
海就从绿变蓝。
and the sea turns from green to blue.

29
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:00,920
秘鲁渔民早就发现，这事常在圣诞节前后出现，
Peruvian fishers noticed it often came around Christmas,

30
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:03,410
所以叫它“圣婴”，厄尔尼诺。
so they called it El Niño, the Christ child.

31
00:01:03,410 --> 00:01:04,320
小鳀表示：
Andy says:

32
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:05,720
这礼物我不要。
no thanks to that gift.

33
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,540
反转二：一点点升温，
Twist two: how can a little warming

34
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:09,480
为什么能搅动全世界？
shake up the whole world?

35
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:10,690
暖水跑到哪儿，
Wherever the warm water goes,

36
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:12,710
水汽和大雨就跟到哪儿。
the moisture and big storms follow.

37
00:01:12,710 --> 00:01:15,050
大气就像被挪了暖气片的房间，
The atmosphere is like a room where someone moved the radiator:

38
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:17,350
整屋的空气都跟着重新流动。
all the air starts flowing differently.

39
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:18,420
这次有多强？
How strong is this one?

40
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:22,250
9月21日，关键海区比常年高了3.05度。
On September 21, the key ocean region was 3.05 degrees above normal.

41
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:24,570
按我国标准，超过2.5度，
By China's national standard, anything above 2.5 degrees

42
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:26,300
就叫超强厄尔尼诺。
counts as a super El Niño.

43
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:29,440
美国海洋大气局估计，打破纪录的概率
NOAA puts the chance of breaking the record

44
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:30,670
大约75%。
at about 75%.

45
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:32,830
峰值预计在11月到12月，
The peak is expected in November or December,

46
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:34,620
很可能拖到明年春天。
likely lasting into next spring.

47
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:36,920
关你啥事？第一：全球会更热。
Why care? First: the whole planet gets hotter.

48
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:41,640
2016年和2024年两个最热纪录，都紧跟着强厄尔尼诺。
The record hot years 2016 and 2024 both followed strong El Niños.

49
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:44,820
第二：天气会乱。按气象部门的经验，
Second: weather gets weird. Forecasters' experience says

50
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:47,750
我国冬天常常偏暖，南方雨偏多。
Chinese winters tend to run warm, with more rain in the south.

51
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:49,620
1998年长江大洪水，
The great 1998 Yangtze flood

52
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:52,470
就发生在上一次超强厄尔尼诺之后。
came right after an earlier super El Niño.

53
00:01:52,470 --> 00:01:54,270
反转三：最强，不等于
Twist three: strongest doesn't automatically mean

54
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:56,740
它是被气候变暖“养大”的。
climate change made it stronger.

55
00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:59,400
哈佛的科学家提醒，一次破纪录，
A Harvard scientist warns one record-breaker

56
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,940
还证明不了这个。
can't prove that on its own.

57
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:03,700
可它叠加在一个本来就变暖的地球上，
But it rides on top of an already warmer planet,

58
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,280
热浪的起点更高了。
so heat waves start from a higher floor.

59
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:07,850
友情提示：这些都是概率预报，
Friendly fine print: these are probability forecasts,

60
00:02:07,850 --> 00:02:09,260
不是板上钉钉。
not certainties.

61
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:11,500
厄尔尼诺不等于一定发洪水，
El Niño doesn't guarantee floods.

62
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:14,370
还要看季风、副热带高压这些角色。
Monsoons and other weather systems get a say too.

63
00:02:14,370 --> 00:02:16,490
气象部门每个月都会更新，
Weather agencies update every month,

64
00:02:16,490 --> 00:02:18,380
跟着官方预报走就好。
so follow the official forecasts.

65
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:21,010
等信风重新吹起来，冷水回来，
When the trade winds pick up again and the cold water returns,

66
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:22,260
海又会变绿。
the sea turns green again.

67
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:24,060
小鳀现在只盼一件事：
Andy is waiting for one thing:

68
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:27,120
它的妹妹拉尼娜，快点回家做饭。
his sister La Niña to come home and cook.

